## What is upstream content

Everything under `skills/diagram-design/` is copied from the upstream
repository by `scripts/sync-skills.mjs`:

| Path | Files | Contents |
|---|---|---|
| `SKILL.md` | 1 | philosophy, type selection, connector rules, taste gate |
| `references/` | 60 | the 42 type references plus primitives, import, export, style guide |
| `assets/` | 177 | templates, per-type examples in three variants, gallery, icon set |
| `scripts/` | 5 | draw.io / Mermaid / Excalidraw extractors, self-check, SVG export |

Upstream prose is not edited, translated, or reordered; line endings are
normalized to LF, which is what upstream stores for the entry file (its
`.gitattributes` pins `SKILL.md` to `eol=lf`). `upstream.json` records the exact
version, commit, file list, and content digest.

`skills/diagram-design/scripts/` here is upstream content, not this port's
tooling: `SKILL.md` invokes those Python helpers. The port's own sync tool lives
at the package root in `scripts/`.

## What this port adds

`cordis.patch.yml`, `package.json`, `scripts/`, `locale/`, `icon.svg`,
`README.md`, and this file are the port itself and are offered under the same
MIT terms.

## What was left out

The upstream repository's other host surfaces are not vendored: its
`.claude-plugin/`, `.codex-plugin/`, `.factory-plugin/`, and `.agents/`
manifests, its `commands/` and `prompts/` slash-command templates, its `docs/`
tree, and its own CI scripts. DeepSeek Harness reaches the same flows through
the skill body itself plus its own user-invoked command registry; the vendored
`references/` and `assets/` are complete, so nothing the skill routes to at run
time is missing.
